{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"logo":1},{"createdAt":2,"updatedAt":3,"Logo":4},"2022-12-10T11:21:49.842Z","2023-07-21T12:06:33.099Z",{"data":5},{"id":6,"attributes":7},50,{"name":8,"alternativeText":9,"caption":9,"width":10,"height":11,"formats":12,"hash":32,"ext":14,"mime":17,"size":33,"url":34,"previewUrl":9,"provider":35,"provider_metadata":36,"createdAt":37,"updatedAt":37},"LOGO_KaPt_only.png",null,750,233,{"small":13,"thumbnail":24},{"ext":14,"url":15,"hash":16,"mime":17,"name":18,"path":9,"size":19,"width":20,"height":21,"provider_metadata":22},".png","https://res.cloudinary.com/dizcp5ddf/image/upload/v1689941180/small_LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3.png","small_LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3","image/png","small_LOGO_KaPt_only.png",25.96,500,155,{"public_id":16,"resource_type":23},"image",{"ext":14,"url":25,"hash":26,"mime":17,"name":27,"path":9,"size":28,"width":29,"height":30,"provider_metadata":31},"https://res.cloudinary.com/dizcp5ddf/image/upload/v1689941180/thumbnail_LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3.png","thumbnail_LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3","thumbnail_LOGO_KaPt_only.png",6.14,245,76,{"public_id":26,"resource_type":23},"LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3",20.1,"https://res.cloudinary.com/dizcp5ddf/image/upload/v1689941180/LOGO_Ka_Pt_only_ab2158b9e3.png","cloudinary",{"public_id":32,"resource_type":23},"2023-07-21T12:06:20.758Z"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"project":1},{"Nom":2,"Localisation":3,"Programme":4,"Surface":5,"Description":6,"createdAt":7,"updatedAt":8,"publishedAt":9,"locale":10,"Images":11,"localizations":361},"The revived Aguedal","Morocco","Hospitality",4500,"The resort reimagines the Aguedal- “enclosed meadow” in Amazigh - a vast aristocratic garden, where relaxation areas and amenities abound at the threshold of a traditional Moroccan walled city. Sprawling across hectares this Aguedal seamlessly blends relaxation with design. The journey begins with a staged descent toward the lake, passing through a protective buffer zone of service and farm buildings. These structures, arrayed along the road like a fortified wall, humbly echo the historic ramparts of Taza, Fez, and Meknes.\n\nThrough the linear embrace of orchards, the \"Kasbah\" emerges, a green ceramic “qoubba” crowning its panoramic jetty. As the heart of the resort’s public programs, the Public Kasbah is firmly rooted in the hillside, separating two realms: one cultivated and verdant, the other untamed, shifting with the seasons from lush green to ochre. Its horizontal design draws the eye toward the lake, while shadowed terraces and low-rise steps create layered outdoor retreats. These transitions provide access to the resort’s various functions, centering around a dynamic core where the lobby, café, and qoubba interconnect.\n\nLight, air, and views flow through the Kasbah in deliberate choreography. Spaces harness cardinal orientations and prevailing winds, creating framed perspectives that reveal the landscape’s beauty and drama.\n\nBeyond the Kasbah’s vibrancy, the residential units embrace quietude. The villas to the northwest and lodges to the east respond to the terrain, evoking the troglodyte dwellings of nearby Bahlil. Tucked into the earth and accessed through landscaped trenches, these homes are turned inward and open exclusively to the lake’s serenity. Private patios and solar chimneys weave the interior spaces back into the Aguedal’s fabric, blending privacy with connectivity.\n","2025-03-20T11:52:35.534Z","2025-03-20T11:58:40.407Z","2025-03-20T11:58:40.339Z","en",{"data":12},[13,76,129,174,219,271,316],{"id":14,"attributes":15},123,{"name":16,"alternativeText":17,"caption":17,"width":18,"height":19,"formats":20,"hash":69,"ext":22,"mime":25,"size":70,"url":71,"previewUrl":17,"provider":72,"provider_metadata":73,"createdAt":74,"updatedAt":75},"© KAPT Studio",null,6769,9002,{"large":21,"small":33,"medium":42,"xlarge":51,"thumbnail":60},{"ext":22,"url":23,"hash":24,"mime":25,"name":26,"path":17,"size":27,"width":28,"height":29,"